  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual command to identify racists",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'hands up all racists who support white genocide' because the meme implicitly commands the viewer to perform the action of raising hands (as depicted visually) to identify and condemn individuals based on race and alleged support for a false conspiracy theory. This creates a direct, participatory projection where the viewer is expected to mentally or physically align with the action, making them an active participant in the hateful framing. The deictic nature is implicit in the command structure of the text, which addresses the viewer as the one who should execute the gesture to 'identify' racists.",
